    "basis": [
      "jinshu:053:s0108 and s0111–s0118 explicitly identify Sun Xiu 孫秀 as Sima Lun’s strategist, addressed by Sima Ya and Xu Chao in the plot against Jia; the adviser counsels delaying restoration of the deposed prince. zizhitongjian:083:s0226–s0244 and s0263 repeat this distinctive proposal, the refusal to restore the prince first, the forged-letter strategy and the eventual Jia coup. jinshu:031:s0584 places the named same adviser beside Lun in that same coup.",
      "zizhitongjian:083:s0282–s0284 continue with Lun’s rewards and Sun Xiu controlling him, followed at s0302–s0351 by Sima Yun’s revolt, forged orders, the Pan Yue/Shi Chong cases and the adviser engineering Lun’s Nine Bestowals and usurpation. jinshu:047:s0278 names Sun Xiu preparing Lun’s usurpation ritual; jinshu:004:s0151–s0158 give the same Lun faction’s fall, Sun Xiu’s execution and his two sons. jinshu:071:s0248/s0251 expressly recall Sun Xiu’s treason and Hui losing authority in the three-prince restoration sequence. No different Sun Xiu is introduced in these governing frames.",
      "jinshu:031:s0607–s0608 and zizhitongjian:083:s0352–s0354 give the distinctive installation of Yang Xuanzhi’s daughter: her maternal grandfather Sun Qi is friendly with Sun Xiu and therefore Xiu establishes her. That shared relationship and action identify both the later Jin031 record and ZZT083p142 as the same court adviser. The false Xiu occurrence at ZZT083s0386 is Li Xiang 李庠 and is expressly excluded from identity proof.",
      "jinshu:028:s0670 and songshu:032:s0194 pair the exact name Sun Xiu with Zhang Lin taking power in the matching Minhuai mulberry-omen retrospective. songshu:060:s0264 explicitly recalls Chen Huai supporting Sun Xiu and disaster reaching Huainan in the earlier Western court, contrasted with the subsequent restoration; it is a retrospective reference to the same Lun adviser, not a later Song contemporary."
    ],
